# **DeerAge Privacy Policy**

**Last updated:** November 15, 2026
**App name:** DeerAge
**Developer:** Trey Harper

---

## **1. Introduction**

DeerAge (“we,” “our,” or “us”) values your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect personal information when you use our mobile application (“the App”). By using the App, you agree to this policy.

---

## **2. Information We Collect**

We collect only the data necessary to provide app functionality, improve performance, and maintain reliability.

### **Personal Information**

| Data Type                             | Purpose of Collection                                                                                     |
| ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Precise Location**                  | Optional. Only while you are using the app, and only if you allow it. DeerAge uses it on the phone to suggest today's hunt region and, if you keep a pre-shot record, to attach the stand. The region name (not the GPS point) is sent with an analysis so the age prior matches the hunt. The GPS point stays on your phone unless you share a record. It is linked to your own records and is not used to track you. DeerAge does not collect location in the background. |
| **Email Address** | Optional. Only if you sign up for rut-timing alerts and an end-of-season recap, or if you type an email on a wrong-call report or a cancel note so we can answer that one note. A report email is used for customer support only, never for marketing, and is not filled in for you. DeerAge does not require an email. |
| **Lease manager name or phone** | Optional. Only if you type them in Settings so a text can be addressed. They stay on this phone. DeerAge does not read your contacts, does not upload the number, and does not send the message. You press Send in Messages. |
| **Push notification token** | Optional. Only if you turn notifications on, so we can send an update or a poll to this install. |
| **Photos or Videos**                  | To allow users to upload deer images for ageing analysis and to store or display these within the app. A submitted wrong-call report keeps that scan's photo so we can study the miss. A second look stores the same photo and the two ages. Those photos are private, linked to the report, kept until the report is resolved plus 1 year, and can be deleted from Messages in Settings. |
| **Wrong-call reports** | If you say a call was wrong or right, DeerAge stores the scan id, the call, the result, an age you type, whether you marked it jawbone-aged, your note, and, for a wrong call, the scan photo. Confirmed harvest ages are copied into the same store so later checks can use them. |
| **Cancel and return notes** | If you answer the cancel survey or the "What could we do better?" prompt, DeerAge stores the reason and the optional note, tied to this install's app user id. |

### **Usage and Diagnostic Information**

| Data Type                                               | Purpose of Collection                                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Other Usage Data**                                    | To understand app feature usage and improve user experience.                                             |
| **Crash Data, Performance Data, Other Diagnostic Data** | To identify and fix technical issues, monitor app stability, and improve performance.                    |
| **Environment Scanning**                                | To analyze surroundings (e.g., lighting or object detection) for photo accuracy in deer ageing features. |

